CC   RepeatMasker Annotations:
CC        Type: LINE
CC        SubType: L1
CC        Species: Takifugu
CC        SearchStages: 
CC        BufferStages:
CC        Description: Both open reading frames of Tx1_FR1 encode
CC                     products closely related to those of Tx1
CC                     in Xenopus laevis. The first (bp 230_1141)
CC                     shows 55% similarity over the N-terminal
CC                     190 AA;  the same region is 34% similar to
CC                     the gag region of the lymphoproliferative
CC                     disease virus. There are more distnat matches
CC                     to GAG-[proteins of all other LTR retrotransposons.
CC                     The pol ORF (pos 1723-5625) is 53% similar
CC                     to the pol product of Xenopus Tx1. The 'composite'
CC                     nature of Tx1 is thus conserved, and does
CC                     not represent a collaboration between two
CC                     transposable elements, as was one hypothesis
CC                     by Garrett et al (Mol Cell Biol 1989 Jul;9(7):3018-27).
CC                     Like the closely related LINE1, multiple
CC                     subfamilies are defined by the 3' UTR and
CC                     Tx_Fur appears to be an old constitutent
CC                     in the Fugu genome.       
