CC                     the consensus, is repeated about 830 times
CC                     in the diploid genome of a female chicken,
CC                     suggesting that nearly the entire terminal
CC                     heterochromatin on the Z chromosome consists
CC                     of this macrosatellite family. Ref: Hori
CC                     T et al Characterization of DNA sequences
CC                     constituting the terminal heterochromatin
CC                     of the chicken Z chromosome. Chromosome Res.
CC                     1996 Sep;4(6):411-26. The current consensus
CC                     contains fragments of interspersed repeats:
CC                     GGLTR7-int (pos 1-2222), GGLTR5B (4271-4777)
CC                     and CR1-F3 (5753-5812). Includes recons consensi
CC                     GG000023, GG000132, GG000131, GG000041, GG000142,
CC                     GG000205, GG000204, GG000563, GG000562, and
CC                     GG000397  erv       
