CC   RepeatMasker Annotations:
CC        Type: SINE
CC        SubType: Core-RTE
CC        Species: Ornithorhynchus
CC        SearchStages: 40,50
CC        BufferStages:45[260-372]
CC        Description: 9% kimura. Core 206-287 matches MAR1 MIRs
CC                     and BovB_Opos best. Pos 143-287 are derived
CC                     from the 5-end of BovB_Plat (pos 142-331),
CC                     pos 288-354 match its 3-end (3257-3329).
CC                     Pos 314-328 (AGAACGACTACAGAT) and 3241-3255
CC                     (AGAAAGGTTGCGGAT) of BovB_Plat are similar
CC                     (and perhaps were identical) so that PlatSINE1
CC                     could have formed by a simple homologous
CC                     recombination. Pos 1-142 are not yet similar
CC                     to anything else. Note that MAR1c_Mdo aligns
CC                     to pos 200-353, as if (1) the SINE would
CC                     have originated before the monotreme/theria
CC                     split or, more likely, the regions in the
CC                     5- and 3-prime ends of the involved LINEs
CC                     are essential for SINE propagation. Indeed,
CC                     the similarity of MAR1c_Mdo to PlatSINE1
CC                     is over 200-262 and 316-354 with a gap in
CC                     Mar1c_Mdo. Possibly this suggests an origin
CC                     of the CORE (and CORE-SINEs in a LINE element.
//
