CC        Description: A non-autonomous Charlie12_GG element that
CC                     had a Mariner1b_GG insertion at pos 2260-1
CC                     and a bp 227-1640 deletion. Reported in chicken
CC                     genome paper. Although suggestive of concurrent
CC                     activity, the sequence is quite (4-5%) diverged
CC                     from the current Charlie12_GG consensus.
CC                     A number of these elements had further co-traveling
CC                     insertions (e.g. a reverse CR1-D LINE (pos
CC                     3793-end) inserted at pos 345). The clear
CC                     TSDs support transposition rather than other
CC                     forms of (e.g. segmental) duplication. This
CC                     sequence may cause havoc in annotation.
