CC   RepeatMasker Annotations:
CC        Type: LINE
CC        SubType: CR1
CC        Species: Passeriformes
CC        SearchStages: 
CC        BufferStages:
CC        Description: 20% subst. Starts at pos ~250. gag 2-1045
CC                     (almost complete), pol 1030-3903, encoding
CC                     proteins 60%/71% and 76%/85% identical/similar
CC                     to the CR1-F encoded gag and pol proteins,
CC                     respectively. Majority of copies (2 of 3)
CC                     have one C at pos 3336-7 and one G at pos
CC                     3356-7 AG, causing a frameshift in the pol
CC                     gene. While the pol ORFs and proteins of
CC                     CR1-J2 and CR1-J1 are very similar (92% from
CC                     1128 to end 3992), the gag region is only
CC                     20% similar, and the enocded proteins are
CC                     distant from each other compared to gags
CC                     from other subfamilies. One or the other
CC                     is therefore the product of a recombination.
CC                     Since Je seems to have a 170 bp insertion
CC                     at the recombination point compared to this
CC                     and other subfamilies, it forms the most
CC                     likely candidate.
//
