XX
XX
CC   RepeatMasker Annotations:
CC        Type: LINE
CC        SubType: RTE-BovB
CC        Species: Mammalia
CC        SearchStages: 60
CC        BufferStages:
CC        Description: Possibly ancestral to Plat_RTE1, from which
CC                     this consensus differs by 20%. ORF: 852-3761
CC                     which matches (besides RTE1_Plat by > 80%)
CC                     the pols of RTEs in Nematostella and Marsupials
CC                     both by 51% (67% similarity). The marsupial
CC                     RTE seems too diverged to be a descendant,
CC                     but it can simply be a poorly constructed
CC                     element.   MamSINE1 was dependent on this
CC                     LINE. It arose from a tRNA joined to pos.
CC                     120-280 of the 5prime UTR, spliced to the
CC                     34 bp tail of MamRTE1 (3770-3803). This pattern
CC                     is commonly observed for other RTE-SINE pairs.
CC                     Subfamilies clearly existed, but have not
CC                     been explored yet. Pos 3371-3607 once had
CC                     the tag "X3_LINE". MamRTE1 either was active
CC                     during speciation from monotremes, and was
CC                     more active in that lineage, or a related
CC                     element entered monotremes. The first possibility
CC                     is more likely, as only a fraction (less
CC                     than half) of MamRTE1 elements show in the
CC                     reconstructed mammalian ancestor.  
//
