CC   RepeatMasker Annotations:
CC        Type: LINE
CC        SubType: Penelope
CC        Species: Tetrapoda
CC        SearchStages: 60
CC        BufferStages:
CC        Description: The final third or fourth of a Penelope probably
CC                     active some 350 million years ago. Some conserved
CC                     copies found in Xenopus, over 250 each in
CC                     alligator and turtle, over 125 in chicken,
CC                     and about 100 recognizable in platypus and
CC                     our boreoeutherian ancestor. The ORF from
CC                     pos 2-946 encodes a protein 57% similar (39%
CC                     identical) to AA 690-1006 (end) of Neptune1_Nv_pol.
CC                     The last 130 bp are likely to be a terminal
CC                     direct repeat, though the other end is obviously
CC                     not yet defined. Part of the coding region
CC                     (current pos 182-463) were originally named
CC                     UCON13 as it appeared in a number of ultraconserved
CC                     regions.
