CC   REP131 DNA
XX
DE   RepbaseID: 
XX
KW   DNA/.
XX
XX
CC   RepeatMasker Annotations:
CC        Type: DNA
CC        SubType: 
CC        Species: Sauropsida
CC        SearchStages: 60
CC        BufferStages:
CC        Description: Hairpin with a ~700 bp loop. Termini do not
CC                     match a known DNA transposon yet. Forward
CC                     and reverse may have more differences than
CC                     reflected in the consensus. At least two
CC                     subs appear clear, but they could reflect
CC                     the unresolved forward and reverse stems.
CC                     Long G-rich (and subsequently C-rich) regions
CC                     and secondary repeats make this both a trap
CC                     for false matches and provide a very strong
CC                     secondary structure when transcribed. In
CC                     turtles, crocodiles and birds. Apparently
CC                     not in mammals. Matches a rearranged MIR
CC                     (best to MIRc and MIR_Aves1/2) at 1888-1992,
CC                     2221-2358, and 2121-2220 in the loop area.
CC                     It matches Eulor9A at 1558-1681 and corresponding
CC                     positions 2699-2576. Perhaps functionally
CC                     most significant, pos 1-193 contains basically
CC                     the entire current consensus of the Amniote-wide
CC                     or mammalian-specific element MER131, after
CC                     which REP131 is named. The terminal 230 bp
CC                     also match one end of UCON60_Saur. Fragments
CC                     were previously represented by my REP-1_Croc
CC                     (1242-3004) and REP-540_Croc (1-484 and 4209-3726).
CC                     For mammals, REP131 is in the MIRs stage
CC                     because of the matches to elements in that
CC                     stage.
//
