CC   RepeatMasker Annotations:
CC        Type: DNA
CC        SubType: hAT-Ac
CC        Species: Tetrapoda
CC        SearchStages: 60
CC        BufferStages:
CC        Description: Ancient Activator-like hAT. A few ultra-conserved
CC                     bits of it are aligned with Xenopus in the
CC                     UCSC browser (e.g. chr18:73,792,505-73,792,771).
CC                     Ends still undefined, especially the beginning.
CC                     Almost complete (N-term missing) transposase
CC                     encoded by ORF 188-2498 with a (possible)
CC                     intron at 2064:2139. It is not closely related
CC                     to other elements in RepBase yet. Currently
CC                     closest (up to 32% identical and 50% similar)
CC                     are  HAT-10_XT and  HAT-9_XT in Xenopus and
CC                     some elements found in a crocodilian ancestor
CC                     (hAT-4_AMi, hAT-17_Crp, hAT-2_Crp). Fragments
CC                     of AmnhAT1 were identified as UCON95 (pos
CC                     1732-1872) and UCON102 (2401-2503). The final
CC                     300 bp occur in UCON1, which may have been
CC                     a transposable amalgamate of TEs.
